<!--
  RBM mode's gear of Commander Battle's Battanian troop classes (cb_mpclassdivisions_battania.xml), read by
  CommanderBattle/RbmLoadouts.cs in place of the classes' mp_ gear when the host turns RBM mode on. Same rules as the
  class's own characters (cb_mpcharacters_battania.xml):
  - One Class per MPHeroClass id. Hero is the commander's gear; Troop holds the bots' rosters. Bots draw every slot
    from a random roster, so each slot holds the same kind of item in every roster: the rosters vary the looks (armour,
    helmets and capes of one tier), never the loadout. Weapons, shield, horse and harness are the same in every roster.
  - Setup N replaces weapon setup perk N of the class (index 0 is the class's own loadout and has no entry). Each slot
    mirrors one AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn of the perk; no id empties the slot (pike and falx clear the shield, swords,
    axes and falxes clear the sidearm).
  - Slots: Item0 main weapon (or bow, or javelins), Item1 shield (or arrows), Item2 sidearm (Battanian swords for the
    spears, pikes, lances and javelins; the archers' two-handed sidearm), Item3 free, Cape cloaks and shoulder pieces in
    every roster. Mounted classes carry a horse and harness in every roster; foot classes none.
  - Items only from the singleplayer and RBM item files that RBM.Multiplayer loads in multiplayer (no mp_ items, no
    looter or Nord items), mostly the ones RBM's troop overhaul (RBMCombat_unit_overhaul.xml) gives Battanian troops,
    so they carry RBM's stats. Shields are the plain ids, not RBM's _shoulder copies: those use RBM's own holsters,
    which multiplayer doesn't load.
  - Doctrine: the best longbows (war longbows, the heaviest draw weights), javelin skirmishers, pikes and falxes, the
    fastest infantry. No heavy cavalry and the lightest heavy infantry: the armour sits a step below Vlandia and Sturgia
    at each weight.
  - Gear tiers: light = clan levy (woodland outfits, leather scale, fur and studded leather helmets, targes, a short
    broadsword); medium = trained and picked clan warriors (Battanian mail, cheek-guard helmets, reinforced targes, a
    broadsword); heavy = oathsworn and fians (Battanian scale and noble armour, noble helmets, mail shoulders, the
    culture's best blades and the strongest longbows). The fians stay a step below the oathsworn.
  - No Battanian lance in the singleplayer items: the couched lances (highland horseman, general) are the Sturgian
    lance, the nearest northern one; RBM's own Battanian horsemen carry spears that cannot couch.
  - Seeds (SP troop of the same role and tier in RBM's overhaul):
      clan spearman      battanian_clanwarrior, battanian_volunteer; pike from battanian_trained_warrior, javelins
                         from battanian_scout
      highland warrior   battanian_trained_warrior, battanian_picked_warrior; long falx from battanian_falxman,
                         javelins from battanian_wildling
      highland horseman  battanian_scout, battanian_horseman; javelins and long falx from
                         battanian_mounted_skirmisher
      oathsworn          battanian_oathsworn; spear and blade from battanian_wildling, rhomphaia from
                         battanian_veteran_falxman
      clan archer        battanian_militia_archer, battanian_highborn_youth (two-handed axe); heavy bow from
                         battanian_hero
      fian               battanian_fian (armour, lighter scale than RBM's), battanian_fian_champion (bows, arrows,
                         two-handed blade)
      highland raider    battanian_scout, with clan levy armour (battanian_clanwarrior)
      general            battanian_horseman, battanian_fian_champion (warlord armour)
-->
